{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5950,
  "title": "Start Markdown headings at level 2",
  "body": "> Fixes #4940\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Changed\n\n- 💥 Changed [#4940](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/issues/4940), Markdown headings start at level 2 in each message, set the new `styleOptions.markdownHeadingLevelStartAt` to change it, also for Adaptive Cards headings, in PR [#5950](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5950), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nMarkdown `#` rendered `<h1>`, although the page owns level one. Each message's top heading now renders at the new style option (default `2`), others keep their depth and look.\n\n## Design\n\n- The top heading moves to the start level instead of shifting all levels, so `##` stays `<h2>`; while streaming, levels can change if a higher heading arrives later.\n- Runs on the whole message after the HTML content transform (which streams per block); micromark has no heading option.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `headingLevelDocumentMod.ts`: moves headings, beyond 6 with `aria-level`; `.spec.ts` with invalid classes\n- Adaptive Cards: `textBlock.headingLevel` follows the option, no nested headings\n- `markdown/headingLevels.html`: levels 2–7, snapshot 1 as before\n- `headingLevels.startAt.html`: levels 3–8\n- `headingLevels.startsAtLevel2.html`: `##`, `###` stay 2, 3\n- `adaptiveCard/headingLevel.markdownInHeading.html`: one heading\n- `headingLevel.startAt.html`: level 3\n- `markdownStreaming.html`: TODO says why its skip stays\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [x] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
